### Logistic regression analysis of missingness

-   This techniques is used to assess the association between the probability of missingness with the observed variables.

-   The missingness is modeled using the `indicator variable` mentioned above.

-   The indicator variable can be created manually or by using the `naniar::add_shadow()` function:

    -   Manually:




        ::: {.cell}

        ```{.r .cell-code}
        pollutionlevels %>%
          mutate(
            noise_NA = factor(
              case_when(
        is.na(noise) ~ NA,            # Missing
        TRUE ~ !NA                    # Non-missing
              ),
              levels = c("non-missing", "missing")
            )
          ) %>%
          head()
        ```

        ::: {.cell-output .cell-output-stdout}

        ```
             light    visual     noise air noise_NA
        1 17.66350 0.3293645 111.93033  87     <NA>
        2 16.00311 0.2985631 108.20592 175     <NA>
        3 19.06365 0.5962447 134.58058 103     <NA>
        4 16.08429 0.2018016  76.26353 195     <NA>
        5 16.38814 0.7246732        NA 262     <NA>
        6 21.72910 0.9132740  72.60283 234     <NA>
        ```


        :::
        :::




    -   Using `naniar::add_shadow()`:




        ::: {.cell}

        ```{.r .cell-code}
        pollutionlevels %>%
          add_shadow(noise) %>%
